The '''Black Spire Ruins''',<ref name="Galaxy's Edge 5">[[Galaxy's Edge 5|''Galaxy's Edge'' 5]]</ref> called the '''old post''' by locals,<ref name="GEStaff">{{GEStaff|Black Spire Outpost|themed land}}</ref> or '''old outpost''',<ref name="Galactic Explorer's Guide">''[[Star Wars: The Galactic Explorer's Guide]]''</ref> or simply referred to as the '''ancient ruins''', were located at the edge of [[Black Spire Outpost]] on the [[planet]] [[Batuu]]. Belonging to an ancient settlement<ref name="GE:BS" /> and formerly the original outpost,<ref name="Black Spire">{{SW|url=news/star-wars-galaxys-edge-black-spire-exclusive-excerpt|text=Leia Has a Mission for Vi Moradi in ''Star Wars: Galaxy's Edge - Black Spire'' - Exclusive Excerpt}}</ref> the ruins were at one time the site of a temporary [[Resistance]] [[Resistance Supply|encampment]], which the Resistance picked largely because it had been ideal for their needs.<ref name="GE:BS" /> The encampment included a [[DF.12 Com Turret]]<ref name="D23">{{SW|url=news/d23-doug-chiang-interview-star-wars-themed-land-disney-parks|text=D23 2017: Doug Chiang Talks Designing ''Star Wars''-Themed Land for Disney Parks}} - Text from a display of the model</ref> at an entrance that led directly into the ruins and into caves which included ancient artifacts and worship sites. The Resistance built their control center inside, in some cases cutting through rock to widen the caves.<ref name="Rise of the Resistance">{{GEAttr|Rise of the Resistance|''Rise of the Resistance''}}</ref>

==History==
On a mission from [[General]] [[Leia Skywalker Organa Solo|Leia Organa Solo]] in [[34 ABY]], [[Vi Moradi]] scouted the location, and after she received permission from [[Oga Garra]], she began arrangements for a temporary Resistance base. Thanks to local superstition and the variety of dangerous fauna, the site was often unobserved.<ref name="GE:BS" />

Later, several Resistance recruits were once scrambled there alongside [[BB-8]] and [[Poe Dameron]]. The recruits, [[Bek|Lt. Bek]], and [[Nien Nunb]], boarded a Resistance [[Intersystem Transport Ship]] docked in their open air hangar alongside Dameron's [[T-70 X-wing starfighter|X-wing]]. From nearby, two more Resistance fighters rose from the base, [[Blue Five (Batuu)|Blue Five]] and [[Red Two (Batuu)|Red Two]], to provide wing support. Unknowingly unprepared for the coming [[Battle of Batuu|space battle]] with the [[First Order]], the group departed from the ruins on a mission to the primary Resistance base before the vessel's capture and eventual escape from a Star Destroyer.<ref name="Rise of the Resistance" />

==Behind the scenes==
[[File:ResistanceCamp-GalaxysEdge5.jpg|left|thumb|220x220px|The resistance camp in the ruins]]
The Black Spire Ruins on Batuu were revealed in concept art and as part of the [[Star Wars: Galaxy's Edge|''Star Wars'': Galaxy's Edge]] model revealed by Disney during the theme park area's development and construction, with [[Doug Chiang]] giving some details about it in his interview. This area was believed to be the location of the entrance for ''[[Star Wars: Rise of the Resistance]]'' and later promotional material confirmed it.<ref name="EW Rise">{{WebCite|url=https://ew.com/movies/2019/02/28/star-wars-actors-will-appear-in-disneys-rise-of-the-resistance-ride|text=Star Wars actors bring their characters to life in Disney theme parks' Rise of the Resistance ride|author=Breznican, Anthony|date=2019-02-27|archivedate=20190914091306}}</ref> It was also present on a trading card titled "NEW RECRUITS RENDEZVOUS AT THE ANCIENT RUINS" issued at the Galactic Nights event on [[December 16]], [[2017]] that gave details about the ride and revealed that the location acted as a staging area for the Resistance, including BB-8.<ref name="WDWNewsToday">{{WebCite|url=https://wdwnt.com/2018/01/photos-star-wars-galaxys-edge-trading-cards-provide-new-details-guests-will-find-batuu-2019|text=PHOTOS: Star Wars – Galaxy's Edge Trading Cards Provide New Details of What Guests Will Find on Batuu in 2019|work=WDW News Today|archivedate=20180510032057}}</ref>

